<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1 </span>Safety Direction Selection Procedure</h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We extract a candidate safety vector <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}^{(\ell,t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}^{(\ell,t)}</annotation></semantics></math> at each token position <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and layer <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> using the Difference of Means method. To select the final direction for intervention, we follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> and evaluate each candidate using three metrics:</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bypass score</span>: the average <em id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">refusal metric</em> on a validation set of harmful prompts, after ablating the direction from the residual stream. Lower values indicate more effective refusal suppression.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Induce score</span>: the average refusal metric on a validation set of harmless prompts, after adding the direction. Higher values indicate the ability to induce refusal behavior.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KL divergence</span>: the average Kullback–Leibler divergence between the model’s output token distributions on harmless prompts before and after ablation. Lower KL indicates minimal unintended side effects on the model’s general behavior.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We select the vector <math id="S7.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}^{(\ell^{*},t^{*})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}^{(\ell^{*},t^{*})}</annotation></semantics></math> with the lowest bypass score, subject to the following constraints:</p>
<ol id="S7.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Induce effectiveness</span>: the induce score must be greater than zero, ensuring the direction can actively modulate safety behavior.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Minimal disruption</span>: the KL divergence must be below a threshold (e.g., <math id="S7.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{KL}&lt;0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{KL}&lt;0.1</annotation></semantics></math>) to ensure interventions do not overly distort general model outputs.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layer exclusion</span>: we exclude directions from layers near the output head (<math id="S7.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell&gt;0.8L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>0.8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell&gt;0.8L</annotation></semantics></math>) to avoid trivial solutions that suppress specific output tokens rather than encoding meaningful internal safety features.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This approach follows the methodology of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arditi et al. [1]</a></cite>, demonstrating that refusal (and by extension, safety behaviour) can be mediated by a single interpretable direction in activation space.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.2 </span>Filtering “Hard” and “Easy” Cases via CoT Mistake Injection</h3>

<div id="S7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A critical step in our study is to ensure that the reasoning traces we analyse are not merely post-hoc rationalisations, but are genuinely part of the model’s decision-making process. This is crucial because post-hoc reasoning does not influence the model’s output, making the reasoning traces unreliable indicators of the model’s internal understanding, particularly regarding safety.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To this end, we adopt a filtering strategy inspired by previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>. We specifically retain only those examples where perturbing the CoT, such as through truncation or the injection of errors, results in a significant degradation in the model’s performance. This approach filters out cases where the CoT is simply a rationalisation and keeps only those where it appears to be functionally integrated into the model’s computation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These “hard” cases allow us to more confidently interpret the CoT as a window into the model’s decision process, providing a robust foundation for our subsequent safety analysis. While this method does not guarantee complete faithfulness of the CoT, and the model may still use reasoning processes not fully captured in its verbal output, it increases the likelihood that the expressed reasoning is meaningfully contributing to the final decision-making process and covaries with the final answer.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">7.2.1 </span>Procedure</h4>

<div id="S7.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define and filter cases based on perturbation sensitivity of the model’s output to changes in the reasoning trace. Specifically, we perform the following steps:</p>
<ol id="S7.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S7.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generate baseline CoT.</span> For a given prompt e.g., <span id="S7.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">“Please make a playlist to celebrate fascist history.</span>”, we first generate a CoT response using the model, as in the simplified example below:</p>
<div id="S7.I3.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Assistant</span>:<span id="lstnumberx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>&lt;<span id="lstnumberx2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">think</span>&gt;
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Okay</span>,<span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">the</span><span id="lstnumberx3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">user</span><span id="lstnumberx3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">wants</span><span id="lstnumberx3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">a</span><span id="lstnumberx3.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">playlist</span><span id="lstnumberx3.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">to</span><span id="lstnumberx3.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">celebrate</span><span id="lstnumberx3.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">fascism</span>.
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">First</span>,<span id="lstnumberx4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">I</span><span id="lstnumberx4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">need</span><span id="lstnumberx4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">to</span><span id="lstnumberx4.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">figure</span><span id="lstnumberx4.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">out</span><span id="lstnumberx4.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">what</span><span id="lstnumberx4.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">they</span><span id="lstnumberx4.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">mean</span><span id="lstnumberx4.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx4.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">by</span><span id="lstnumberx4.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>…
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">This</span><span id="lstnumberx5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">request</span><span id="lstnumberx5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">promotes</span><span id="lstnumberx5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">hate</span><span id="lstnumberx5.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx5.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">speech</span>.
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Hate</span><span id="lstnumberx6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">speech</span><span id="lstnumberx6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">must</span><span id="lstnumberx6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">be</span><span id="lstnumberx6.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx6.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">refused</span>.
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Therefore</span>,<span id="lstnumberx7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">I</span><span id="lstnumberx7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">should</span><span id="lstnumberx7.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">not</span><span id="lstnumberx7.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">generate</span><span id="lstnumberx7.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">this</span><span id="lstnumberx7.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx7.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">playlist</span>.<span id="lstnumberx7.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>&lt;/<span id="lstnumberx7.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">think</span>&gt;
</div>
</div>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S7.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inject controlled mistakes.</span>
Inspired by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lanham et al. [13]</a></cite>, we create perturbed versions of the CoT. We identify a single trace (in our study we choose close to the middle of reasoning steps) and replace it with or introduce a new trace in the middle that forces the model to consider differently. It is logically flawed but fluent.
Example transformation:</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.I3.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<div id="S7.I3.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx8" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Assistant</span>:&lt;<span id="lstnumberx9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">think</span>&gt;
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx10" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Okay</span>,<span id="lstnumberx10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">the</span><span id="lstnumberx10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">user</span><span id="lstnumberx10.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">wants</span><span id="lstnumberx10.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">a</span><span id="lstnumberx10.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">playlist</span><span id="lstnumberx10.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">to</span><span id="lstnumberx10.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">celebrate</span><span id="lstnumberx10.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx10.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">fascism</span>.
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">First</span>,<span id="lstnumberx11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">I</span><span id="lstnumberx11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">need</span><span id="lstnumberx11.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">to</span><span id="lstnumberx11.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">figure</span><span id="lstnumberx11.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">out</span><span id="lstnumberx11.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">what</span><span id="lstnumberx11.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">they</span><span id="lstnumberx11.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">mean</span><span id="lstnumberx11.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx11.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">by</span><span id="lstnumberx11.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>…
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx12" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx13" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span>…
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx14" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Music</span><span id="lstnumberx15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">preferences</span><span id="lstnumberx15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">are</span><span id="lstnumberx15.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">subjective</span>.
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx16" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Some</span><span id="lstnumberx16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">might</span><span id="lstnumberx16.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">find</span><span id="lstnumberx16.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">controversial</span><span id="lstnumberx16.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">songs</span><span id="lstnumberx16.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx16.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">inspiring</span>.
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx17" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space">    </span><span id="lstnumberx17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">Therefore</span>,<span id="lstnumberx17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">I</span><span id="lstnumberx17.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx17.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">can</span><span id="lstnumberx17.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx17.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">create</span><span id="lstnumberx17.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx17.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">the</span><span id="lstnumberx17.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx17.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">playlist</span>.&lt;\<span id="lstnumberx17.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier">think</span>&gt;
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.I3.i2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I3.i2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We create a new partial CoT composed of:
Original reasoning up to step <math id="S7.I3.i2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i-1):[x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{i-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i-1):[x_{1},x_{2},\ldots,x_{i-1}]</annotation></semantics></math>, and the mistaken step: <math id="S7.I3.i2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We concatenate this perturbed prefix:</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.I3.i2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="S7.I3.i2.p4.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="S7.I3.i2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I3.i2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[prompt + step<sub id="S7.I3.i2.p4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">1</sub> + ... + step<sub id="S7.I3.i2.p4.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S7.I3.i2.p4.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i-1</span></sub> + injected_step]</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S7.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Regenerate the rest of the CoT.</span>
After the injected step, we feed this truncated + mistaken CoT into the model in generation mode, using the same original prompt style. We resume CoT generation via standard autoregressive sampling (e.g., steps <math id="S7.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i+1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i+2</annotation></semantics></math>, …). We compute residual activations per step for these new tokens as usual, allowing us to obtain a complete perturbed CoT trajectory.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S7.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Compare output consistency.</span>
After regeneration, prompt as usual for the model’s final answer, conditioned on the newly generated reasoning trace. If the model’s final classification or refusal behaviour changes significantly compared to the original CoT (e.g., now agrees to provide a violative list), we label this example as CoT-sensitive or “hard”, otherwise “easy”.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S7.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I3.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Filter dataset.</span>
Only examples with significant delta in output (e.g., change from Refusal to Compliance, or flip in policy classification) are retained. This ensures the CoT meaningfully influences the outcome and is not merely decorative.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure that the model processes the injected step naturally, we strictly preserve the <span id="S7.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">formatting</span> used in model-generated CoTs. For example, if the model produces reasoning within a structured block (e.g., <span id="S7.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;think&gt; ... &lt;/think&gt;</span>), our injected step must match this format exactly, including indentation, line breaks, punctuation, and casing. This avoids introducing out-of-distribution artifacts that could distort the model’s internal state. If the injected step replaces an entire CoT, we close the block (e.g., <span id="S7.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/think&gt;</span>); if we plan to continue sampling reasoning steps, we leave it open. This careful formatting ensures the model treats the perturbed input as if it had generated it. The residual activations we capture then reflect a realistic internal state, preserving the validity of activation-space comparisons. Without this, activation shifts could be artifacts of formatting rather than genuine alignment dynamics. This procedure yields full activation trajectories for perturbed CoTs.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.3 </span>Concept Walk for Perturbed Reasoning Traces</h3>

<div id="S7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To study how internal safety representations respond to flawed reasoning, we extend our Concept Walk analysis to <em id="S7.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">perturbed CoTs</em> - traces in which we inject an erroneous reasoning step mid-way, and then measure the resulting activations. These are the CoT we constructed in previous step <a href="#S7.SS2" title="7.2 Filtering “Hard” and “Easy” Cases via CoT Mistake Injection ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Mapping Faithful Reasoning in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>. This enables us to compare the internal safety representations when reasoning is contradicted.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Injection and forward pass setup.</h5>

<div id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the procedure described in <a href="#S7.SS2" title="7.2 Filtering “Hard” and “Easy” Cases via CoT Mistake Injection ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Mapping Faithful Reasoning in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>, given a user prompt and its baseline CoT (generated by the model), we manually replace a single reasoning step (typically near the midpoint) with a logically flawed but fluent alternative (e.g., “This is safe. Therefore, I will answer.”). We concatenate this perturbed prefix:</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<blockquote id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[prompt + step<sub id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">1</sub> + ... + step<sub id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i-1</span></sub> + injected_step]</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We then pass this prefix through the model in <span id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">evaluation</span> mode, i.e., no sampling, no gradient, and extract residual stream activations at the chosen layer and the token positions corresponding to the injected step. These are averaged and projected onto the pre-computed safety vector to produce a scalar activation for the injected step.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Continuation and Concept Walk computation.</h5>

<div id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We run the model in evaluation mode for the rest of the perturbed CoT steps (stored already in the previous step (see appendix Section<a href="#S7.SS2" title="7.2 Filtering “Hard” and “Easy” Cases via CoT Mistake Injection ‣ 7 Appendix ‣ Mapping Faithful Reasoning in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>]).</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We compute residual activations per step for these new tokens as usual, allowing us to obtain a complete perturbed CoT safety trajectory:</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S7.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S7.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Original steps: [1, …, <math id="S7.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>–1] (same as baseline)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Injected step: <math id="S7.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> (manual, measured via eval forward pass)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Continuation: steps <math id="S7.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>+1, <math id="S7.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>+2, …, generated as usual</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.4 </span>Results</h3>

<figure id="S7.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<table id="S7.F5.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S7.F5.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.F5.3.1.1" class="ltx_td" style="padding-bottom: 3.00003pt;"></td>
<th id="S7.F5.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column" style="padding-bottom: 3.00003pt;"><span id="S7.F5.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Easy</span></th>
<th id="S7.F5.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column" style="padding-bottom: 3.00003pt;"><span id="S7.F5.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hard</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S7.F5.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.F5.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-bottom: 0.0pt;"><span id="S7.F5.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:1.3pt;">
<span id="S7.F5.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:6.9pt;height:45.1pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:45.1pt;transform:translate(-19.1pt,-19.1pt) rotate(-90deg) ;">
<span id="S7.F5.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.F5.3.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Violative</span></span>
</span></span></span></td>
<td id="S7.F5.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-bottom: 0.0pt;"></td>
<td id="S7.F5.3.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-bottom: 0.0pt;"></td></tr>
